Using the addition rule:
$$\begin{align*}
P(A\cup B)&=P(A)+P(B)-P(A\cap B)\\
\frac{3}{4}&=\frac{3}{5}+\frac{1}{4}-P(A\cap B)\\
P(A\cap B)&=\frac{1}{10}
\end{align*}$$
$$\begin{align*}
P(A'\cap B)&=P(B)-P(A\cap B)\\
P(A'\cap B)&=\frac{1}{4}-\frac{1}{10}\\
P(A'\cap B)&=\frac{3}{20}
\end{align*}$$

